cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Flexilearn: a configuration-driven PyTorch training framework"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Hesam
    family-names: Haddad
    alias: TheDoubleH
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-5468-6484"
repository-code: "https://github.com/DoubleH7/flexilearn"
url: "https://github.com/DoubleH7/flexilearn"
abstract: >-
  Flexilearn is a modular, configuration-driven training framework built on
  PyTorch. Models, optimizers, datasets, preprocessing stages, losses and
  training tasks are registered with decorators and wired together entirely
  from a single config.yml, so swapping a component requires no code changes.
  It provides config-hash run identity, selective checkpointing, gradient
  accumulation, MLflow experiment tracking and a simulation-as-data-source
  abstraction for closed-loop evaluation.
keywords:
  - pytorch
